  "title": "Darius I",
  "summary": "Darius I took the Persian throne in 522 BCE and ruled until his death in 486 BCE. He put down revolts, reorganised the empire into twenty satrapies, and began building Persepolis. EBSCO credits him with a royal road of 1,677 miles (2,705 km) with messenger stations. His own inscription at Behistun is a main source for his rise.",
